    "Community" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the Community screen",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Community is a public space: anyone using Pixel Deck can see what you share.\n\n• Share only art you made or have the right to share.\n• Nothing hateful, violent, sexual, harassing or otherwise objectionable, in art, titles or nicknames. There is no tolerance for objectionable content or abusive users.\n• Don't share personal details: no real names, addresses, phone numbers or links.\n\nAnyone can report a post. A post reported by several people is hidden for everyone, and reports are reviewed within 24 hours; content that breaks these rules is removed, and people who break them are blocked from posting. You can block anyone so you don't see their posts, and you can delete your own posts at any time from Mine.\n\nRemix copies a post into your own gallery. Please credit the original artist if you share a remix." : {
      "comment" : "The text of the community rules.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Community is busy right now. Try again in a minute." : {
      "comment" : "Error message when posting to Community is busy.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Community is for ages 13 and up" : {
      "comment" : "A message displayed when the user is under 13 and can't access Community.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Community is full right now. Try again later." : {

    },
    "Community is optional. If you share a sprite to Community, its art, the title and the nickname you choose are published in Pixel Deck's public CloudKit database, hosted by Apple, where anyone using the app can see and copy them. CloudKit links each post to an anonymous identifier for your iCloud account (not your name or email), so you can delete your posts and others can block or report them. Hearts you give and reports you make are stored the same way, and each post shows how many hearts it has. You can delete your posts at any time from Community, Mine. Posts that break the community rules are removed. The developer can see public posts and reports, and uses them only to run and moderate Community." : {
      "comment" : "Privacy policy text.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
